BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_315053618@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260619T050842Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260621T120000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write - South Asheville 
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\nCoworking for write
 rs in your area!\nJoin us for some focused writing time. All writers and a
 ll experience levels are welcome and don’t worry\, no one will see what 
 you've written. This session is about getting your writing done and meetin
 g other writers in your area.\n\nPlease arrive a few minutes early to say 
 hello to everyone\, grab a drink\, and get your writing tools ready. Once 
 everyone’s arrived\, I will lead quick introductions and then set the ti
 mer for our quiet and focused writing session.\n\nAfterward\, we’ll have
  time to chat and get to know each other. We often talk about our successe
 s and challenges as writers. If you don’t have time to stick around\, no
  worries!\n\nA note about the format\nWe don’t host critiques or reading
 s. These events are a safe space for writers of all skill levels and genre
 s to work on their craft\, so no one will read or critique your writing.\n
 \nFor our full event schedule\, visit https://shutupwrite.com\n\nOther Imp
 ortant Details:\n\nVenue Guidelines: Please thank our hosts by purchasing 
 something.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/315053
 618/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260601T141119Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260601T141119Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_315073238@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260619T050842Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T153000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® in Candler/West Asheville
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\nPlease join me and 
 other local writers for a group writing session. Bring whatever you're wor
 king on and grab a coffee\, and we will write alongside each other.\n\nThi
 s is not a critique group\, but we do have short social periods before and
  after writing.\n\\-\\-\\-\nMany have mentioned that The Dripolator is a l
 ittle hard to find if you've never been before. The coffeeshop is located 
 in a strip mall where the Candler YMCA is\, and the sonic. The Dripolator 
 is next to the bank\, and looks a little like a house. There is usually pl
 enty of parking in the lot out front. If you're having trouble send me a m
 essage!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/315073
 238/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260602T181205Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260602T181205Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_315093064@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260619T050842Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260623T193000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® - Downtown
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\n***\\*\\*\\*Please 
 note: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this M
 eetup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\n**Here's how it works
 .** Show up at or before 6:00. At 6:00\, we do some quick introductions. A
 fterward\, for a full 60 minutes (I'll set a timer!) we are heads-down wri
 ting. Writing what? A novel? You bet. Some poetry? Sure. Song lyrics? Your
  resume? That report you need to get to your boss before 8 AM or you'll *n
 eed* *to write* that resume? All of the above and more. Just shut up and w
 rite.\n\nSurrounding ourselves with other writers who are busy putting wor
 ds onto page (physical or virtual) keeps us all accountable and focused.\n
 \nWhen the timer goes off\, we'll check-in with each other and see how it 
 went. Afterward\, feel free to stay to chat and get to know your fellow wr
 iters\, or keep writing\, or take off.\n\nSocializing is optional and will
  happen after (or briefly before) the focused writing. This is a safe spac
 e to work on your craft. No one will read or critique your writing.\n\nFor
  more information about our events\, visit [https://shutupwrite.com](https
 ://shutupwrite.com).\n\n**What to Expect**\n\n* Roughly 15 minutes of intr
 oductions\n* 60 minutes of focused writing (somebody set a timer)!\n* Afte
 rward\, optional socializing\n\n**Being late is okay:** Just show up and g
 et settled\, then check in with the host after the session. (Look for the 
 person with the Shut Up & Write sign).\n\n**What Should I Bring?**\n\n* Wh
 atever you need to be able to write!\n* Earbuds/earplugs if you want to bl
 ock ambient noise.\n\n**Other Important Details:**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Please n
 ote: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this Me
 etup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night e
 vents here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www.
 shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\nHOSTS: This is a multi
 -host event\, so most of the time there will be a host present. If we are 
 unlucky and no host can attend\, please find each other and self-organize.
  Pay attention to the event chat and comments to see who is available.\n\n
 WI-FI: Yes!\n\nPARKING: Street parking in metered spots is free after 6pm.
  Closest municipal garages ($2/hour) are Wall St. & Coxe Street/Sears Alle
 y.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/315093
 064/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260603T222033Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260603T222033Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
